Let me tell you the story behind the name “favicon”.

🌐 The story of Favicon

Imagine it is around the year 1999.

People are starting to use the internet, and web browsers show many websites. Microsoft introduced a feature in Internet Explorer 5 to help websites have a small identifying icon.

The idea was:

“Every website should have its own small favorite icon.”

At that time, users could save websites as Favorites in Internet Explorer.

For example:

⭐ Google
⭐ Yahoo
⭐ Amazon

When a user saved a website in their Favorites list, the website could provide a small icon next to its name.

So Microsoft used the name:

FAVorites + ICON = FAVICON
FAVorites
   +
ICON
   ↓
FAVICON

That's where the name came from. 🎉

==========

📅 When was favicon introduced?

1999 — with Internet Explorer 5.

The original idea was mainly for the browser's Favorites/Bookmarks list.

Later, other browsers adopted the idea, and favicons started appearing in:

Browser tabs
Bookmarks
Favorites
Browser history
Mobile home-screen shortcuts
Website shortcuts

