Why does the browser ask for /favicon.ico?

Because of this historical convention from early browsers.

The browser basically says:

"Let me check whether this website has a file called:

/favicon.ico"

So it requests:

https://yourwebsite.com/favicon.ico

If it finds it:

200 OK ✅

It displays the icon.

If it doesn't find it:

404 Not Found ⚠️

Then you see the error in Developer Tools.

